# Implementation Plan - Product Hardening Pass (Approved)

This plan outlines the final implementation to remove all demo/mock/fallback behavior from the application, forcing only real database-backed workflows in production.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Portal Guard (hooks.server.ts):** Portal guard will block only protected app routes (e.g. `/dashboard`, `/chat`, `/persona-config`, `/calendar`, etc.). Route endpoints like `/login`, `/signup`, health checks, and static files will render normally. If Supabase is unconfigured, protected routes render a detailed setup page (unless `ALLOW_DEMO_MODE` is set to `'true'`).
> - **ALLOW_DEMO_MODE Security:** The `ALLOW_DEMO_MODE` flag will be a private server-only variable (`$env/dynamic/private`). The client will receive this configuration state via the server layout load data, keeping the flag hidden from public client scripts.
> - **Direct Persona Creation API:** We will create a dedicated `/api/agents` POST route for direct persona creation, avoiding mixing database writes with the external account factory engine path.
> - **Safe Ticket Preservation:** Before deleting an agent, SvelteKit will manually update all assigned Kanban tickets to set `assignee_agent_id = NULL`, guaranteeing data preservation regardless of DB cascade definitions.
> - **Social Handle Sync Protection:** The connection sync will not overwrite the agent's core `handle`. Connected platform handles will remain local to the connection metrics card.

